00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:28.500
To really understand a Taiwan defense budget, you have to see it as a signal inside a security

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:31.040
relationship that was never written down as a treaty.

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:36.700
A common misunderstanding treats every extra military dollar as simple preparation for a war.

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:41.740
The same dollar can also be a message to a partner that has no legal duty to show up.

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:46.600
The United States switched official diplomatic relations from Taipei to Beijing nearly

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:47.640
50 years ago.

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:51.340
That switch did not create a mutual defense treaty with the island.

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:56.700
Because no such treaty exists, armed sales and a forward American presence are political

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:59.200
choices, not automatic obligations.

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:02.640
Each of those choices has a domestic cost in Washington.

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:05.980
Visible self-help by Taipei lowers that cost.

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:11.460
Legislators who want to approve weapons or keep forces nearby can point to an island that

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:13.100
is already funding its own defense.

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:17.760
stance. Without that evidence, the same legislators are more exposed to the charge that they

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:22.540
are underwriting someone else's risk. That is the mechanism, public spending as proof

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:28.160
of seriousness, which then makes outside support easier to sustain. An informal security

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:33.680
tie has to be re-earned in politics, a treaty would have done that work in advance. Self-help

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:38.580
is the currency that relationship runs on. So when claims arrive that the spending is only

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:42.920
a provocation, or only a shield, look at the rationale on the page.

